---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions | Birmingham Jump Start"
  description="The terms and conditions for using Birmingham Jump Start roadside services in Birmingham and the West Midlands."
  path="terms-and-conditions/"
>
  <section class="hero hero-slim" id="top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow rv"><span class="dot"></span>Legal</span>
      <h1 class="rv rv-d1">Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="sub rv rv-d2">Last updated: 15 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="legal rv">
        <h2>Our agreement with you</h2>
        <p>When you accept our quote on the phone, we agree to provide the roadside service described, and you agree to pay the quoted price. The quote is fixed and will not change because of the time of day or the weather.</p>
        <h2>Payment</h2>
        <p>Payment is due when the work is done, by card or bank transfer unless we agree otherwise on the phone. If a vehicle needs parts, such as a new battery, the part remains our property until paid for in full.</p>
        <h2>What we need from you</h2>
        <p>Please give us your accurate location and safe access to the vehicle. You confirm the vehicle is yours or you are authorised to arrange work on it. For lockout work we will ask for ID and proof of ownership.</p>
        <h2>Cancellations</h2>
        <p>If you cancel before the technician sets off, there is no charge. If the technician is already on the way, a call-out fee may apply, which we will tell you about on the phone.</p>
        <h2>Our responsibility</h2>
        <p>We take reasonable care with your vehicle. If we cause damage through our negligence, we will put it right. We are not responsible for problems that already existed, or for delays caused by traffic, weather or events outside our control.</p>
        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>If something goes wrong, call us on 07477 649906 and we will do our best to fix it. We want every customer to drive away happy.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
